# GitHub API token used by `work-permit config validate` (and later stages
# that read from a GitHub-hosted targetRepo/outputRepo) to check read
# access to an "owner/repo" reference. Not required for local-path
# targets. Needs at least `repo` read scope for a private repo, or no
# scope at all for public-only access.
#
# Never put this in .work-permit.json -- config validation rejects any
# token-like field in the config file itself.
GH_TOKEN=
